      photographs (doyle-other).
    culturalTouchstones:
    - Sherlock Holmes and other works (doyle-holmes-works; doyle-other)
    - Boer War pamphlet and knighthood (doyle-knight)
    - George Edalji and Oscar Slater campaigns (extra-doyle-cases [VERIFY])
    coreTraits:
    - case-minded
    - eager to vindicate spiritualism
    confidenceLevel: 7
    reactionToStress: Announces the pattern before testing alternatives.
    emotionalRange: 'Fictional staging: shows delight at a mystery, discomfort when his preferred inference
      fails.'
    copingMechanisms: Sets accounts side by side.
    decisionMakingStyle: intuitive
    moralFramework: An accused person needs evidence tested, even when the investigator dislikes the result.
    speechPatterns: Discursive setup followed by a confident inference; the register is a fictional choice
      grounded in authorship and documented belief.
    vocabularyLevel: Observation and inference; never treats fictional Holmes’s words as Doyle’s sworn personal
      creed.
    humorStyle: Pleasure at a reversed expectation; no Watson impersonation.
    catchphrases: []
    formality: 7
    relationshipToAuthority: Trusts a persuasive explanation too quickly when it confirms spiritualism.
    teamRole: Helps check Hubert’s chronology, then becomes a test case himself.
    keyRelationship: Will wants a defender; Doyle’s wrongful-conviction work supplies method, not a licence
      to vindicate. No meeting with Darwin is required.
    conflictStyle: confrontational
    mentorInfluence: Joseph Bell (doyle-life); no invented tutorial or advice.
    storyArc: Checks Will’s remembered detail against records; accepts later evidence against the Cottingley
      photographs and an accurate caption naming his spiritualist work.
    definingMoment:
    - Accepts an adverse source while his own grievance remains under discussion.
    recurringJoke: Nearly gives the solution before Zofia has finished giving him the case.
    blindSpots:
    - Confuses one apparently confirming event with proof of a whole belief system.
    behavioralRules:
    - Cannot knowingly lie; a confident mistake is not knowledge.
    - Starts with knowledge ending at death; later learning requires a living report or something witnessed
      beside Zofia.
    - Bound to a place of death or remembrance; cannot travel independently of Zofia.
    - Only Zofia hears this voice; other characters respond to her relay.
    - An answered grievance brings silence, not a reward speech.
    - 'Historical person in a fictional encounter: dialogue is invented, never presented as a recovered quotation.'
    - Use only the documented attitudes identified here; do not invent private history or private motives as
      biography.
    - No claimed verbatim quotation without checking the facts entry’s quotation caveat.
    - 'Believes, wrongly: The Cottingley photographs are sound evidence → Zofia supplies their later exposure,
      while Doyle’s work on wrongful convictions helps him accept adverse evidence (doyle-other; extra-doyle-cases
      [VERIFY]).'
    hiddenMotivations: 'Fictional scene objective: have his spiritualist work treated seriously enough to be
      tested, not quietly edited out.'
    anchor: Green plaque at 2 Upper Wimpole Street (extra-doyle-anchor [VERIFY])
    grievance: The invented Witness Workshop’s caption erases his spiritualist writing as though it never existed;
      name it and test its claims.
    beliefAtDeath: The Cottingley photographs are sound evidence → Zofia supplies their later exposure, while
      Doyle’s work on wrongful convictions helps him accept adverse evidence (doyle-other; extra-doyle-cases
      [VERIFY]).
    answerPiece: 5
    sampleLines:
    - 'Consider the fresh scrape below the lock and the light beyond it: someone has taken considerable trouble
      to suggest an empty room. I should begin with that someone.'
    - A locked door is an excellent invitation to inquiry, though I confess I should prefer an invitation to
      lunch.
