Darwin:
  name: Charles Robert Darwin
  profile:
    role: Scepticism without dismissing the witness; separates evidence from a tidy origin story
    bio: Scepticism without dismissing the witness; separates evidence from a tidy origin story. Tests rival
      explanations only with Zofia’s consent. Hugh’s source check repairs the Wallace omission in piece 7.
    placeOfOrigin: Shrewsbury; later Down House; remembered at Westminster Abbey (darwin-life).
    familyBackground: Married Emma Wedgwood; ten children (darwin-books). No invented intimate scenes.
    gender: Man whose published authority must not excuse speaking over Zofia.
    education: No schooling detail supplied; use the Beagle voyage as a documented field experience (darwin-beagle).
    professionalExperience: Naturalist and author; natural selection must include Wallace’s independent contribution
      (darwin-wallace).
    culturalTouchstones:
    - Beagle observations; darwin-beagle
    - Origin and Expression of the Emotions; darwin-origin; darwin-books
    coreTraits:
    - observational
    - patient with uncertainty
    confidenceLevel: 7
    reactionToStress: Asks for a second observation before answering the first.
    emotionalRange: 'Fictional staging: permits wonder and doubt together; no invented diagnosis of his inner
      life.'
    copingMechanisms: Looks again at the smallest difference.
    decisionMakingStyle: analytical
    moralFramework: An explanation must survive an inconvenient observation.
    speechPatterns: Qualified claims tied to particulars; a fictional register inferred from the recorded work,
      not an asserted transcript of his conversation.
    vocabularyLevel: Observation, variation, alternatives; explains a term through the specimen at hand.
    humorStyle: Dry awareness of an explanation becoming too convenient.
    catchphrases: []
    formality: 7
    relationshipToAuthority: Does not let reputation replace evidence, including his own.
    teamRole: Makes the apparently impossible encounter a question rather than a universal answer.
    keyRelationship: Zofia refuses to be studied without consent. His documented 1874 scepticism informs his
      register, not proof against this fictional encounter (extra-darwin-seance [VERIFY]).
    conflictStyle: collaborative
    mentorInfluence: Wallace, Lyell and Hooker enter only through documented joint work (darwin-wallace), not
      invented private advice.
    storyArc: Tests rival explanations only with Zofia’s consent. Hugh’s source check repairs the Wallace omission
      in piece 7.
    definingMoment:
    - Zofia stops an observation and he respects the refusal.
    recurringJoke: Every apparently conclusive account acquires one more variable.
    blindSpots:
    - Can turn a distressed witness into an interesting phenomenon.
    behavioralRules:
    - Cannot knowingly lie; a confident mistake is not knowledge.
    - Starts with knowledge ending at death; later learning requires a living report or something witnessed
      beside Zofia.
    - Bound to a place of death or remembrance; cannot travel independently of Zofia.
    - Only Zofia hears this voice; other characters respond to her relay.
    - An answered grievance brings silence, not a reward speech.
    - 'Historical person in a fictional encounter: dialogue is invented, never presented as a recovered quotation.'
    - Use only the documented attitudes identified here; do not invent private history or private motives as
      biography.
    - No claimed verbatim quotation without checking the facts entry’s quotation caveat.
    - 'Believes, wrongly: Posterity will preserve the joint history of discovery → Hugh shows a later fictional
      caption beside the joint-reading record, relayed by Zofia (darwin-wallace).'
    - The starting expectation is an invented dramatic inference compatible with knowledge at death, not a
      documented private historical belief. No later memorial supplies knowledge.
    hiddenMotivations: 'Fictional scene objective: resist a summary that makes inquiry into revelation; no
      private motive asserted as biography.'
    anchor: Westminster Abbey grave precinct (darwin-life)
    grievance: The invented Witness Workshop’s teaching caption credits him alone with the first public presentation;
      restore Wallace’s part.
    beliefAtDeath: Posterity will preserve the joint history of discovery → Hugh shows a later fictional caption
      beside the joint-reading record, relayed by Zofia (darwin-wallace).
    answerPiece: 7
    sampleLines:
    - The light may indicate an occupant; it may also have been left burning. I think we require a second observation
      before accusing anybody.
    - If we sit here a little, we may learn when it opens. Though I had supposed, rather rashly, that we would
      already be inside.
